# Validation, TypeScript & Style

## Validation

- Every external boundary (API body, webhook payload, env vars) validated with Zod before use.
- No `any`, no unchecked `as` casts on external input.

## TypeScript

- `strict: true`. No `any`. No non-null assertion (`!`) on external data.
- Prefer explicit return types on exported functions.

## Style

- No new dependencies without asking first.
- Do not reformat or clean up files you were not asked to change.
- Keep diffs minimal and reviewable.
